# ==============================================================================
# BLOCK 1: METADATA BLOCK
# ( Version Control Exclusion Manifest, Invariant Ignore Rules & Cognitive Scope )
# ==============================================================================
# Project:     OmniCode Language Engine & Bare-Metal OS
# File:        .gitignore
# Scope:       Repository-wide version control exclusions
#
# PURPOSE & ARCHITECTURAL PHILOSOPHY:
#   This exclusion manifest defines the formal boundary between permanent,
#   version-controlled source assets and transient, ephemeral build, execution,
#   or host-environment artifacts.
#
# WHY EXTENSIVE COMMENTING MATTERS FOR AI AGENTS & DEVELOPERS:
#   1. Guardrails for Automated AI Commits:
#      Autonomous coding agents frequently run `git add .` or stage files during
#      automated pipelines. Without explicit semantic categorization, an AI might
#      accidentally commit multi-gigabyte QEMU disk images (`.iso`, `.img`),
#      ephemeral REPL command histories containing private prompts (`.omnicode_history`),
#      or compiler cache artifacts.
#   2. Preventing Destructive Deletion of Exclusion Rules:
#      When an AI or developer seeks to clean up "unused" gitignore rules, detailed
#      comments explain non-obvious requirements (e.g. why `*.iso` is ignored even
#      though OmniCode builds an OS kernel: ISOs are build outputs, not source code).
#   3. Explicit Boundary Between Source and Artifacts:
#      Ensures that human collaborators and automated agents preserve clean git
#      trees, minimizing repository bloat and eliminating cross-platform noise.
# ==============================================================================


# ==============================================================================
# BLOCK 2: OPENING BLOCK
# ( Compiler Intermediates, Build Targets & Dependency Caches )
# ==============================================================================
# RATIONALE:
#   - Rust and LLVM produce extensive intermediate representations (IR), object
#     files, incremental cache databases, and native ELF/PE binaries during compilation.
#   - These must never be tracked in version control.
# ==============================================================================

# Rust compiler target directory (contains debug, release, and cross-target artifacts)
/target/
target/

# Compiler object files, static archives, and dynamic shared libraries
*.o
*.a
*.rlib
*.so
*.dylib
*.dll

# Cargo incremental build caches and backup manifests
*.cargo-ok
*.orig


# ==============================================================================
# BLOCK 3: BODY BLOCK
# ( Bare-Metal Disk Images, Packaging Bundles, REPL History & Emulation Stubs )
# ==============================================================================
# RATIONALE:
#   - Bare-Metal & Emulation:
#     QEMU and xorriso generate raw bootable media (ISOs, raw binary disk images,
#     and QCOW2 copy-on-write overlays) during bare-metal kernel development.
#   - Editor Extensions:
#     VS Code extension packaging produces binary .vsix bundles via @vscode/vsce.
#   - Interactive Session Telemetry:
#     The OmniCode REPL persists interactive user command history to `.omnicode_history`.
#     This file contains local developer keystrokes and must remain strictly untracked.
#   - Debugger History:
# ==============================================================================
# Native distribution tarballs and installers
dist/*.tar.gz
dist/*.zip
!dist/.gitkeep
infra/dist/*.tar.gz
infra/dist/*.zip
!infra/dist/.gitkeep
**/dist/*.tar.gz
**/dist/*.zip
!**/dist/.gitkeep

# Bare-metal kernel bootable ISOs, disk images, and QEMU virtual disk formats
*.iso
*.bin
*_bin
*.img
*.qcow2
*.elf
*.efi
*.EFI

# ==============================================================================
# BLOCK 4: RUNTIME STATE, EPISODIC MEMORIES & LOGS
# ==============================================================================
# Inscribed neural-symbolic execution traces and episodic logs
*.scroll
*.log
!*.omni
!*.tape
storage/scrolls/**
**/storage/scrolls/**
runtime/scrolls/**
**/scrolls/**
!**/scrolls/**/.gitkeep
!**/storage/scrolls/**/.gitkeep

# Neural brain weight checkpoints & plasticity cache
*.weights
storage/weights/
**/storage/weights/

# Interactive REPL session history (local terminal command history)
.omnicode_history
.gdb_history

# Process crash core dumps
/core
/core.*
core.[0-9]*
vgcore.*

# ==============================================================================
# BLOCK 5: APPS, EDITORS & DEPENDENCY CACHES
# ==============================================================================
# VS Code packaged extension archives
apps/editors/vscode/*.vsix
editors/vscode/*.vsix
*.vsix

# Node.js dependency trees and npm package caches
node_modules/
.npm/

# Python virtual environments & bytecode caches
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
.venv/
env/
venv/
.oci-cli/

# ==============================================================================
# BLOCK 6: ENVIRONMENT SECRETS & CLOUD CREDENTIALS
# ==============================================================================
# Local environment variables and tokens (NEVER commit live secrets)
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
!.env.example

# Temporary cloudflare or test logs
*.log
!*.omni

# Temporary, swap, and backup editor files
*.swp
*.swo
*~
*.tmp
*.bak


# ==============================================================================
# BLOCK 4: CLOSING BLOCK
# ( Host Operating System Overrides, Local IDE State & Workspace Seal )
# ==============================================================================
# RATIONALE:
#   - Local developer workstations produce OS-level desktop database caches
#     and editor-specific window state that are irrelevant to other collaborators.
#   - Local environment configuration overrides must not leak across developers.
#
# INVARIANT BOUNDARY GUARANTEE:
#   - All canonical source reels in `examples/*.omni`, standard library modules in
#     `lib/core/*.omni`, specification docs in `docs/`, and tests in `tests/`
#     MUST remain tracked, deterministic, and clean.
# ==============================================================================

# macOS desktop services metadata, spotlight caches, and trash folders
.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes

# Windows Explorer thumbnail databases and desktop configurations
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini

# Local IDE configuration caches (preserve .vscode/settings.json)
.idea/
*.sublime-workspace
.vscode/*.log
.vscode/.browse.*
